{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.LrTensorCharacterBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.LrTensorCharacterBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Sigma","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.trivialModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.trivialModel","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L194-L207","doc":"The class axiomatisation is **consistent** (no `sorry` introduced):\na trivial model with an empty tuple index, where both sides are `0`,\ninhabits the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lr_tensor_character_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lr_tensor_character_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L165-L192","doc":"**LR comultiplication bridge for Hecke characters**\n(`cor:lr-tensor-character-bridge`), conditional on the class per\n§3b-cond.  For every irreducible block `ν ⊢ Σ n_i` and every\ntensor-product braid `β = ⊗_i β_i`, the `H_n`-character of `β` equals\nthe iterated Littlewood–Richardson sum of the per-factor characters:\n\n  χ^ν_{H_n}(β_1 ⊗ … ⊗ β_k)\n    = Σ_{(λ_1, …, λ_k)} c^ν_{λ_1,…,λ_k} · Π_i χ^{λ_i}_{H_{n_i}}(β_i).\n\n**Derived, not assumed.**  The class supplies the sum over the\nmultiplicity space; the LR coefficient reaches the statement as a\ncoefficient because summing a constant over `Fin c` gives `c • x`.\nThe corollary's content is exactly that step: `c^ν_{λ_1,…,λ_k}` is a\n*count* of copies, not a weight put in by hand. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:lr-tensor-character-bridge","label":"cor:lr-tensor-character-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tensorChar_eq_multiplicitySum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tensorChar_eq_multiplicitySum","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L157-L157","doc":"**The hypothesis: the character is a sum over the multiplicity\nspace.**  Restricting `V_ν` along the parabolic chain\n`H_{n_1} ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ H_{n_k} ↪ H_n` decomposes it into one copy of\n`V_{λ_1} ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ V_{λ_k}` per Littlewood–Richardson tableau, so the\ncharacter is the sum of the per-factor character products over those\ncopies — indexed here by a tuple together with which of its\n`c^ν_{λ_1,…,λ_k}` copies is meant.\n\nThis is the conjectural content, inherited from\n`prop:hecke-branching-trace-decomposition`.  It does **not** state\nthe corollary's identity: that the LR coefficient appears as a\nnumerical weight is derived in `lr_tensor_character_bridge` from the\nfact that it is the number of copies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.factorChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.factorChar","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L143-L143","doc":"Per-tuple product of per-factor characters `Π_i χ^{λ_i}_{H_{n_i}}(β_i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tupleOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tupleOf","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L141-L141","doc":"The partition-tuple `[λ_1, …, λ_k]` named by an index `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tupleFintype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tupleFintype","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L139-L139","doc":"Each tuple-index set is finite. Declared as an instance binder so the\nsigma-indexed multiplicity sum below elaborates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tupleIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tupleIndex","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L136-L136","doc":"Finite index set of LR partition-tuples `(λ_1, …, λ_k)` feeding `ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tensorChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.tensorChar","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L134-L134","doc":"LHS tensor character `χ^ν_{H_n}(β_1 ⊗ … ⊗ β_k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LRTensorCharacterBridge","kind":"class","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L131-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.iteratedLR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.iteratedLR","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L102-L108","doc":"Iterated LR coefficient\n`c^ν_{λ_1, …, λ_k}` defined by left-folded composition of\ntwo-factor coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lrCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.lrCoefficient","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L87-L100","doc":"Littlewood–Richardson coefficient `c^ν_{λ μ}`. Concrete model:\nencodes two structurally-required identities\n\n  c^ν_{λ, ∅} = δ_{ν = λ}     (identity coefficient for empty μ)\n  c^ν_{λ, μ} = 0  whenever  |ν| ≠ |λ| + |μ|    (size additivity)\n\nand falls back to 0 in the remaining (combinatorially non-trivial)\ncases. The genuine combinatorial value is\n`#LR-tableaux(ν / λ; weight μ)`; the stub captures the two\ncleanest invariants that any concrete realisation must respect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.size","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L84-L85","doc":"The size `|λ| = Σ λ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqPartition","kind":"instance","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqPartition.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqPartition.decEq","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartition.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartition.repr","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartition","kind":"instance","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition","kind":"structure","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-tensor-character-bridge.lean#L73-L82","doc":"An *unvalidated* partition representation — a `List ℕ` intended\nto model a partition (non-increasing list of positive naturals)\nbut with no subtype proof enforcing the invariant. Sufficient for\nstating the LR coefficient and the bridge identity at the\nstructural-stub level. The full proof upgrade target should\nreplace this with `Mathlib.Combinatorics.Partition` and propagate\nthe dependent type through the stubs below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}